course: dictionary
lesson: 5156
title: Words that cannot be brought together
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Irreconcilable looks long, but you can break it into pieces. Re means again, and reconcile means to bring things into agreement, or to make friends again after a quarrel. The ir- at the front means not. So irreconcilable means it cannot be brought into agreement.
explain: Read this: «"Irreconcilable differences" is the official reason given for a divorce.» The clue is differences. The two people are so far apart that they can never agree, so the reason is called irreconcilable. Check it: put in cannot be made to agree, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Writers use this word in news, law and history. Countries can have irreconcilable aims, which means they will never want the same thing. In a story, a quarrel called irreconcilable tells you it will never be mended. Look for the phrases irreconcilable differences and irreconcilable views.
fact: Irreconcilable means so different that they can never be made to agree.
fact: Used of people, irreconcilable means they cannot become friends again after a quarrel.
fact: «Irreconcilable differences» is a phrase often used in law and news.
fact: Reconcile means to make things agree, or to become friends again.
fact: The ir- at the start of a word means not, so irreconcilable is the opposite of reconcilable.
exercise: «"Irreconcilable differences" is the official reason given for a divorce.» What does irreconcilable mean here? | Happy and friendly | Written down on paper | Very small and easy to fix | *So different that they can never be made to agree
exercise: Two friends had a quarrel, and now they say their differences are irreconcilable. What does this suggest? | They have already made up and are best friends | They are going on holiday together | *They can never become friends again after the quarrel
exercise: In irreconcilable, what does the ir- mean? | Very | Together | *Not | Again
test: Which words could replace irreconcilable in «irreconcilable views»? | Easy to change | Quite loud | *Impossible to bring into agreement | Hard to see
test: A story says the quarrel between two brothers is irreconcilable. What does that tell you? | The brothers are going on holiday | *The quarrel will never be mended | They will make up by lunchtime | The quarrel was only a joke
exam: Which sentence uses irreconcilable correctly? | The dog ran irreconcilable across the park | *The two countries had irreconcilable aims, so the talks failed | She felt irreconcilable after a long sleep
